{
  "description": "Wire-format facts independently checked from pinned schemas and cached release-class inspection. No proprietary implementation text or disassembly included. These facts are independent of live-server validation.",
  "observations": [
    "Light body: signed VarInt X/Z, four long-array bitsets, two lists of 2048-byte packed-nibble arrays; no trust-edges flag in this scope.",
    "Biome chunk positions: X low 32, Z high 32; each bounded byte buffer is bottom-to-top biome-only palettes. Dimension section count is supplied by caller.",
    "763 named compound NBT permits TAG_End. 764/765 anonymous compounds permit TAG_End. 766+ TRUSTED_COMPOUND_TAG rejects TAG_End/null and non-compound roots, despite stale optional-NBT schemas.",
    "Palette long-array length prefixes disappear at 770. Paper 1.21.5 build 114 still overallocates the removed length prefix in every biome section and sends the resulting exact zero tail; 771+ size calculation and writer-size assertion are corrected.",
    "View/simulation distance constructors/readers use plain signed VarInt scalars without codec-side gameplay clamps.",
    "No registry-ID name database or dimension height is invented."
  ],
